      <div type="clause" n="2.5">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:ICn">I Cn</ref> 2.5</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="2.5" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="282" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ gif<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#ICn_2-5.lnote.oe.1"/> hit þonne to bote gegá, ⁊ se cyningc þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> geþafige, þonne bete man þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> cyricgrið into þære<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#ICn_2-5.lnote.oe.2"/> cyricean be ciningces fullan mundbryce, ⁊ þa my[n]sterclænsunge<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#ICn_2-5.lnote.oe.3"/> begyte, swa þærto gebyrige, ⁊ ægþer ge mægbote ge manbote fullice<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#ICn_2-5.lnote.oe.4"/> gebete, ⁊ wið God<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#ICn_2-5.lnote.oe.5"/> huru þingie georne.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="2.5" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="282" ed="#liebermann"/>And gif hit þonne to bote gega, ⁊ se cyningc þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> geþafige, þonne bete man þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> cyricgriþ into þare cyrican be cyninges fullan mundbrece, ⁊ þas mynstres clansunge begyte, swa ðarto<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#ICn_2-5.lnote.oe.1-5"/> gebyrige, ⁊ ægðær ge mægbote ge manbote fullice gebete, ⁊ wyð Gode huru þingye georne.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="2.5" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="282" ed="#liebermann"/>Si tunc ad emendationem ueniat, et rex ita patiatur, emendet ęcclesię pacem in<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#ICn_2-5.lnote.oe.1-2"/> ipsam ęcclesiam plena regis mundbrice, et reconciliationem ęcclesię requirat<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#ICn_2-5.lnote.oe.2-2"/> (querat), sicut ad eam pertinebit, et mægbotam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#ICn_2-5.lnote.oe.3-2"/> et<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#ICn_2-5.lnote.oe.4-2"/> manbotam plene emendet<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#ICn_2-5.lnote.oe.2-2"/> (reddat), et saltem erga<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#ICn_2-5.lnote.oe.2-2"/> (apud) Deum sedulo<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#ICn_2-5.lnote.oe.5-2"/> componat.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="2.5" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="283" ed="#liebermann"/>Si autem<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#ICn_2-5.lnote.oe.1-4"/> ad<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#ICn_2-5.lnote.oe.2-4"/> emendationem peruenerit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#ICn_2-5.lnote.oe.3-3"/>, et rex hoc permiserit, ante omnia<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#ICn_2-5.lnote.oe.4-3"/> ęcclesię pacem fractam pleniter<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#ICn_2-5.lnote.oe.5-3"/> emendet secundum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#ICn_2-5.lnote.oe.6"/> plenam forisfacturam, quam Angli nominant<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#ICn_2-5.lnote.oe.7"/> múndbrece<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#ICn_2-5.lnote.oe.8"/>, (et<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#ICn_2-5.lnote.oe.9"/>) ęcclesię reconciliationem adquirat, (et<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#ICn_2-5.lnote.oe.9"/>) plenam emendationem parentibus et domino occisi<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#ICn_2-5.lnote.oe.10"/> persoluat, quam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#ICn_2-5.lnote.oe.11"/> Angli mæibote<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#ICn_2-5.lnote.oe.12"/> et<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#ICn_2-5.lnote.oe.13"/> manbote<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#ICn_2-5.lnote.oe.14"/> dicunt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#ICn_2-5.lnote.oe.15"/>, et super omnia Deo satisfaciat<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#ICn_2-5.lnote.oe.16"/> secundum decretum episcopi.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="2.5" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="283" ed="#liebermann"/>Deinde enim debet ipsi ecclesie sue pacis infracturam secundum montam regis, templique purificacionem perquirat secundum illius dignitatem, emendetque tam cognacionis quam hominis emendam plenam, maximeque erga Deum.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="2.5" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="156" ed="#robertson"/>⁊ gif hit þonne to bote gegá ⁊ se cyningc þæt geþafige, þonne bete man þæt cyricgrið into þære cyricean be ciningces fullan mundbryce, ⁊ þa my[n]sterclænsunge<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#ICn_2-5.robnote.fn.2"/> begyte swa þærto gebyrige, ⁊ ægþer ge mægbote ge manbote fullice gebete, ⁊ wið God<ptr type="editorNote" n="3" target="#ICn_2-5.robnote.fn.3"/> huru þingie georne.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="234" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And gif hit þonne to bote gega and se cyningc þæt geþafige, þonne bete man þæt cyricgrið into þære cyricean be ciningces fullan mundbryce, and þa mynsterclænsunge begyte, swa þærto gebyrige, and ægþer ge mægbote ge manbote fullice gebete, and wið God huru þingie georne.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="283" ed="#liebermann"/>Und wenn es nun zur Busszahlung kommt, indem der König dies erlaubt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#missing"/>, dann büsse [jener] Mann den [Bruch des] Sonderfriedens der Kirche an jene [verletzte] Kirche durch vollen [Betrag der Busse für] Bruch des königlichen Sonderschutzes und beschaffe die Kirchenreinigung, wie dazu gehört, und zahle Busse für den [Erschlagenen], sowohl als Verwandten [an die Sippe] wie als Untergebenen [an dessen Herrn], vollständig und sühne vor allem eifrig gegenüber Gott.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And if it then comes to compensation, the king permitting it, let [that] man pay compensation for [breach of] the church's protection to that [violated] church at the full [amount for] breach of the king's protection, and obtain the cleansing of the minster as is fitting, and pay compensation for the [slain man] in full, both as kinsman [to the kindred] and as dependant [to his lord], and above all make eager atonement to God.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="157" ed="#robertson"/>And if it comes to the payment of compensation, and the king allows this course, amends for the violation of the protection of the church shall be made by the payment to the church in question of the full fine for breach of the king's <hi rend="italic">mund</hi>, and the purification of the church shall be carried out as is fitting, and compensation both to the kin and to the lord of the slain man shall be fully paid, and above all supplication shall earnestly be made to God.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="235" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And if it then reaches the point at which compensation may be paid and the king allows it, payment of an amount equal to the full penalty for violating the king’s protection shall be given to the particular church as penance for the violation of the church’s sanctuary, and the cleansing of the church shall take place in the proper manner, and compensation to both the family and lord of the victim shall be fully paid, and most importantly, prayers are to be faithfully offered up to God.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="283"><ref target="clause:VIIIAtr_3">VIII Atr 3</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Vgl. VIII Atr. 3</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="336"><ref target="clause:VIIIAtr_3">VIII Atr 3</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">In G, ‘gif’ was written above the line in another hand. Liebermann compares VIII Atr 3.; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 283, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">þa mynsterclænsunge begyte: þas mynstres clansunge A</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">mynsterclænsunge: mysterclænsunge G</note>
